{"text": "r\u00a2\n\nx\n\n* FROM:\n\nRE\n\nLorillard\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\nSee Distribution\nLaurie Moroz\n\n1982 Switching Study , -\n\n\u2018The purpose of this memo is to inform you of changes which are\nbeing made in the 1982 Switching study.\n\nSUPPLIER\n\n\u2018The research supplier has been changed \u2018from The Data Group, Inc.\nto Ad Factors, Inc. Mr. Joseph Bonner, formerly of The Data\nGroup, will supervise the study at Ad Factors. (The Data Group\nwill provide year-end 1981 tabs, due mid-February). I have\nmonitored interviewing at Ad Factors and I am satisfied that\n\nthe quality and consistency of the field work is being\n\nmaintained.\n\nQUESTIONNAIRE\n\nChanges made in the Switching Study questionnaire, beginning\nJanuary 1982, are as follows:\n\nQuestions on exact and relative tar and nicotine levels\nof respondent's reqular brand (Q.14a,14b,15) have been\ndeleted . They provided little usable information and\nspace was needed for new questions. ong\n\nAn occupation question has been added. This will be\ncoded according to the Census Bureau's standard \u2018\nclassifications.\n\nThe income question was simplified, and the \"under $7500\"\ncategory was eliminated.\nThe series of questions on seven reduced tar brands (Q.15c-g),\nusually asked during the 2nd month of the quarter, has been\nomitted this quarter. Much of the material overlaps with\nthe Corporate AAU, and the responses did not seem to\nchange enough from quarter to quarter to warrant asking\nthe questions so often. (llowever, we will be able to include\nsomething similar in the future, if there is sufficient\nneed or interest).\n\ntTspsz6co",
